  "body": "**Link to problem area**: https://spec.matrix.org/unstable/appendices/#matrixto-navigation\r\n\r\n**Issue**\r\n\r\nThis area contains the following text:\r\n\r\n> The components of the matrix.to URI (`<identifier>` and `<extra parameter>`) are to be percent-encoded as per RFC 3986.\r\n>\r\n> Examples of matrix.to URIs are:\r\n>\r\n> * Room alias: `https://matrix.to/#/%23somewhere%3Aexample.org`\r\n> * Room: `https://matrix.to/#/!somewhere%3Aexample.org`\r\n> * Permalink by room: `https://matrix.to/#/!somewhere%3Aexample.org/%24event%3Aexample.org`\r\n> * Permalink by room alias: `https://matrix.to/#/%23somewhere:example.org/%24event%3Aexample.org`\r\n> * User: `https://matrix.to/#/%40alice%3Aexample.org`\r\n\r\nIn those examples, `!` is not percent-encoded despite being listed by as a reserved character (to be percent-encoded) by RFC 3986: https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3986/#page-13\r\n\r\n**Expected behaviour**\r\n\r\nThe `!`s should be percent-encoded, and ideally the characters to be percent-encoded would be listed directly in the spec because digging up the relevant section from the RFC was not easy.",
